4. THE LIKELIEST PORTING BUG: periodic Hann instead of symmetric.
   `np.hanning` is SYMMETRIC (divides by n-1).  The textbook DSP
   window is PERIODIC (divides by n).  Cost, measured:
   n=16   max|w_sym - w_per| = 1.545085e-01   w_sym[-1]=0.000e+00  w_per[-1]=0.038060
   n=64   max|w_sym - w_per| = 3.787507e-02   w_sym[-1]=0.000e+00  w_per[-1]=0.002408
   n=512  max|w_sym - w_per| = 4.706208e-03   w_sym[-1]=0.000e+00  w_per[-1]=0.000038
   sigpow on the real detail pair: symmetric 5.11913118e+07
                                   periodic  5.12660861e+07
   relative difference 1.4607e-03
   MEASURED: the difference is far larger than the golden-vector
   tolerance below, so a golden vector CATCHES this bug.

5. CHOOSING THE GOLDEN-VECTOR TOLERANCE BY MEASUREMENT.
   Three perturbations that a correct implementation may legitimately
   differ by: f32 input storage, summation order, and FFT plan.
